---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import {fields,factors} from '../../../lib/vending-calculator.mjs';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication',name:'Vending Machine Location & Profit Calculator',url:'https://mercerlanepress.com/tools/vending-machine-profit-calculator/',applicationCategory:'BusinessApplication',operatingSystem:'Any modern web browser',isAccessibleForFree:true,description:'Educational vending machine contribution, break-even, scenario and location assessment calculator.'};
---
<BaseLayout title="Vending Machine Profit Calculator: Location, Break-Even & ROI" description="Free vending machine profit calculator. Compare monthly contribution, break-even sales, equipment recovery and location evidence using your own costs. No signup." schema={schema} sensitiveTool={true}>
 <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'Tools',href:'/tools/'},{name:'Vending Machine Profit Calculator'}]} />
 <header class="wrap page-head"><p class="eyebrow">FREE TOOL · NO SIGNUP</p><h1>Vending Machine Profit Calculator</h1><p class="lede">Look below sales at the costs of operating a machine. Then check whether the location deserves deeper investigation.</p><p>Values below illustrate the manual's hypothetical example. Replace them with your own evidence. They are not industry averages or a sales forecast.</p></header>
 <section class="wrap calc-area" aria-label="Vending calculator"><div class="calc-grid">
 <form id="vending-form" novalidate><h2>Your monthly assumptions</h2><div class="inputs">{fields.map(([id,label,value,min,max,unit])=><label for={id}>{label}<input id={id} name={id} type="number" min={min} max={max} step="any" value={value} required inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="assumptions-note" /></label>)}</div><p id="assumptions-note" class="small">Enter 0 for costs that do not apply. Card share assumes the same average value for cash and card transactions. Percentage commission uses gross sales. Fixed host and payment charges still apply when sales are zero.</p><div class="actions"><button type="reset" class="button button-secondary">Reset illustrative inputs</button><button type="button" id="print" class="button button-secondary">Print</button><button type="button" id="copy" class="button button-secondary">Copy summary</button></div><p id="copy-status" role="status"></p></form>
 <div class="results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><h2>Monthly estimate</h2><div id="validation" role="status"></div><dl id="result-list"></dl><p class="small">Machine operating contribution before wider business overhead and tax. Not take-home income or accounting net profit.</p><p class="small">Excludes equipment depreciation, finance interest and principal, income tax, sales-tax remittance, insurance, storage and administration unless you add the relevant operating cost to “Other direct” or service. Equipment investment is shown separately; initial stock and working inventory are additional startup cash.</p><p class="small">Break-even holds these variable rates and fixed monthly costs constant. Recovery is a simple equipment-cost comparison, without financing or changes in future performance.</p></div>
 </div>
 <details class="advanced"><summary>Compare weak, base and strong cases</summary><p>Change transactions per day and service labour independently. Other assumptions come from the main form. These labels describe your scenarios, not their likelihood.</p><div class="scenario-inputs">{['Weak','Base','Strong'].map((name,i)=><fieldset><legend>{name}</legend><label for={`scenario-t-${i}`}>Transactions / day<input id={`scenario-t-${i}`} type="number" min="0" max="10000" step="any" value={[10,20,35][i]} /></label><label for={`scenario-s-${i}`}>Service labour / month ($)<input id={`scenario-s-${i}`} type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="any" value="100" /></label></fieldset>)}</div><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Scenario comparison (USD)</caption><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Gross sales</th><th>Contribution</th><th>Margin</th><th>Recovery months</th></tr></thead><tbody id="scenarios"></tbody></table></div><p id="scenario-errors" role="status"></p><h3>Commission sensitivity</h3><p>Compare percentage host commission while retaining the fixed payment. Edit each rate to match the terms under discussion.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Base assumptions with different commission rates</caption><thead><tr><th>Commission %</th><th>Host payment</th><th>Contribution</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[0,5,10,15,20].map((rate,i)=><tr><td><label class="sr-only" for={`commission-${i}`}>Commission comparison {i+1} (%)</label><input id={`commission-${i}`} type="number" min="0" max="100" value={rate} step="any" /></td><td id={`host-${i}`}></td><td id={`contribution-${i}`}></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
 <details class="advanced"><summary>Assess the location evidence</summary><p>Score 0 serious weakness, 1 weak, 2 ordinary or uncertain, 3 good, 4 strong, 5 exceptional. Choose UNKNOWN when evidence is missing. A high score is not a sales forecast.</p><div class="inputs">{factors.map((factor,i)=><label for={`factor-${i}`}>{factor}<select id={`factor-${i}`}><option value="UNKNOWN">UNKNOWN</option>{[0,1,2,3,4,5].map(n=><option value={n}>{n}</option>)}</select></label>)}</div><label for="hard-stop">Any unresolved hard-stop concern?<select id="hard-stop"><option value="UNKNOWN">UNKNOWN — not checked</option><option value="YES">YES — issue unresolved</option><option value="NO">NO — checked</option></select></label><p class="small">Check safe installation, placement authority, compliance, security and acceptable commercial terms.</p><p id="qualification-result" role="status"></p><p>48–60: strong candidate for deeper analysis. 38–47: promising, investigate further. 28–37: weak or uncertain. Below 28: normally reject unless substantial new evidence emerges. Incomplete assessments receive no definitive band.</p></details>
 </section>
 <section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap narrow prose"><h2>How to read the result</h2><p>Monthly gross sales = operating days × transactions per day × average transaction value. Contribution subtracts product costs, payment costs, host payment, waste, direct service and travel, maintenance and other direct costs. Stock purchased for later sale is working inventory. It is not automatically a cost of this month's sales.</p><h3>A transparent worked example</h3><p>At 22 operating days, 20 transactions per day and $2.25 per transaction, gross sales are $990. With product cost at 43% ($425.70), payment costs at 5% on all sales ($49.50), commission at 10% ($99), service labour of $100 and $40 total waste and maintenance, contribution is $275.80. A $4,500 installed machine gives a simple comparison of 16.3 months. The same assumptions at 10 transactions per day give $67.90 contribution; at 35 give $587.65.</p><p>The manual rounds its strong case to approximately $587.64. Direct arithmetic on the stated assumptions gives $587.65; this calculator retains that arithmetic.</p><h3>What changes the economics?</h3><p>Sales volume changes the dollars available after variable costs. Fixed host payments create more downside risk at low sales. Per-transaction fees matter more on low-value purchases. Service time, access delays and isolated stops can reduce contribution even where gross sales look attractive.</p><h2>Common questions</h2><details><summary>Is a location score a revenue forecast?</summary><p>No. It organizes evidence about demand, placement, access, terms and route fit. You still need separate sales assumptions and a site survey.</p></details><details><summary>Why is capital recovery unavailable?</summary><p>A machine with zero or negative contribution has no meaningful positive recovery period. Zero equipment investment also does not produce a useful recovery comparison.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use a fixed host payment or cash-only machine?</summary><p>Yes. Set percentage commission to zero and enter the fixed monthly host payment. For cash-only operation set card share to zero. Keep any actual fixed payment charges.</p></details><details><summary>Are my figures saved?</summary><p>No calculator entries are sent to a backend or saved by this tool. Copy or print a summary before closing the page. Existing site analytics consent applies; calculator entries are not included in analytics events.</p></details><details><summary>Does this calculate tax profit?</summary><p>No. It is an educational operating comparison. Use your own accounting records and applicable advice for tax, depreciation and wider business costs.</p></details><h2>Use evidence for the next decision</h2><p><a href="/vending-machine-route/evaluate-vending-machine-location/">Evaluate a proposed location</a>, <a href="/vending-machine-route/vending-machine-economics-before-you-buy/">model machine economics before purchase</a>, and <a href="/vending-machine-route/plan-a-vending-machine-service-route/">plan service around genuine need</a>.</p><p>Want to manage your actual machines, stock, service visits and route profitability? The Mercer Lane Vending Machine Route Operating System is being prepared as a separate Excel product. Purchase details will be added when the product is available.</p><p>Want the full operating method? <a class="text-link" href="/books/the-vending-machine-route-operating-manual/">Explore Warren Holtby's Vending Machine Route Operating Manual</a> or <a href="/vending-machine-route/">read the free vending guides</a>.</p></div></section>
 <noscript><p class="wrap notice">Enable JavaScript to use the interactive calculator. The worked example and guides remain available above.</p></noscript>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
 import {calculate,qualify,fields} from '../../../lib/vending-calculator.mjs';
 const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#vending-form')!;const money=(x:number|null)=>x===null?'Not meaningful':new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD'}).format(x);
 const pct=(x:number|null)=>x===null?'Not meaningful':`${(x*100).toFixed(1)}%`; const months=(x:number|null)=>x===null?'Not meaningful':x.toFixed(1);
 let summary='';
 function update(){const data=Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));const result=calculate(data);document.querySelector('#validation')!.textContent=result.errors.join(' ');document.querySelector('#result-list')!.replaceChildren();
 for(const el of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input'))el.setAttribute('aria-invalid',String(!el.validity.valid));
 summary='';if(!result.errors.length){const pairs=[['Gross sales',money(result.revenue)],['Product costs',money(result.product)],['Payment costs',money(result.cardFees)],['Host payment',money(result.host)],['Service labour',money(result.service)],['Travel',money(result.travel)],['Waste / shrink',money(result.waste)],['Maintenance',money(result.maintenance)],['Other direct costs',money(result.other)],['Operating contribution',money(result.contribution)],['Contribution margin',pct(result.margin)],['Break-even sales',money(result.breakEven)],['Equipment recovery (months)',months(result.recovery)]];for(const [k,v] of pairs){const dt=document.createElement('dt'),dd=document.createElement('dd');dt.textContent=k;dd.textContent=v;document.querySelector('#result-list')!.append(dt,dd)}summary='Vending machine estimate (USD)\n'+fields.map(([key,label])=>`${label}: ${data[String(key)]}`).join('\n')+'\n'+pairs.map(([k,v])=>`${k}: ${v}`).join('\n')+'\nContribution before wider overhead and tax. Educational assumptions, not a forecast.'}
 const rows=document.querySelector('#scenarios')!;rows.replaceChildren();const errors=[];
 ['Weak','Base','Strong'].forEach((name,i)=>{const t=(document.querySelector(`#scenario-t-${i}`) as HTMLInputElement).value,s=(document.querySelector(`#scenario-s-${i}`) as HTMLInputElement).value;const r=calculate({...data,transactions:t,service:s});const tr=document.createElement('tr');const values=r.errors.length?[name,'Check inputs','—','—','—']:[name,money(r.revenue),money(r.contribution),pct(r.margin),months(r.recovery)];values.forEach(v=>{const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=v;tr.append(td)});rows.append(tr);if(r.errors.length)errors.push(`${name}: ${r.errors.join(' ')}`)});document.querySelector('#scenario-errors')!.textContent=errors.join(' ');
 for(let i=0;i<5;i++){const r=calculate({...data,commission:(document.querySelector(`#commission-${i}`) as HTMLInputElement).value});document.querySelector(`#host-${i}`)!.textContent=r.errors.length?'Check inputs':money(r.host);document.querySelector(`#contribution-${i}`)!.textContent=r.errors.length?'Check inputs':money(r.contribution)}
 const q=qualify(Array.from({length:12},(_,i)=>(document.querySelector(`#factor-${i}`) as HTMLSelectElement).value),(document.querySelector('#hard-stop') as HTMLSelectElement).value);document.querySelector('#qualification-result')!.textContent=`Known-score subtotal ${q.total??'—'} / 60; ${q.unknown} UNKNOWN. ${q.message} A strong score does not guarantee profitability.`;
 }
 document.querySelector('.calc-area')!.addEventListener('input',update);form.addEventListener('submit',e=>e.preventDefault());form.addEventListener('reset',()=>{document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('.advanced input').forEach(el=>el.value=el.defaultValue);document.querySelectorAll<HTMLSelectElement>('.advanced select').forEach(el=>el.selectedIndex=0);requestAnimationFrame(update)});document.querySelector('#print')!.addEventListener('click',()=>window.print());document.querySelector('#copy')!.addEventListener('click',async()=>{const status=document.querySelector('#copy-status')!;if(!summary){status.textContent='Correct the inputs before copying.';return}try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(summary);status.textContent='Summary copied.'}catch{status.textContent='Clipboard unavailable. Use Print to retain the summary.'}});update();
</script>
<style>
 .calc-area{padding-bottom:3rem}.calc-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,.8fr);gap:2rem;align-items:start}.inputs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem}label{display:grid;gap:.3rem;font-size:.94rem;font-weight:650}input,select{width:100%;padding:.65rem .7rem;font:inherit;color:var(--ink);background:#fff;border:1px solid #75828f;border-radius:3px;min-height:44px}input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #087f9c;outline-offset:3px}input[aria-invalid=true]{border:2px solid #a12710}.results{padding:1.6rem;background:var(--paper);border-top:4px solid var(--cyan)}dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:.5rem 1rem}dt,dd{margin:0}dd{text-align:right;font-weight:700}dt:nth-last-of-type(4),dd:nth-last-of-type(4){border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:.8rem;color:var(--navy)}.small{font-size:.85rem;margin-top:1rem}.advanced{margin-top:2rem;padding:1.25rem;border:1px solid var(--line)}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy)}.advanced[open] summary{margin-bottom:1rem}.scenario-inputs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}fieldset{border:1px solid var(--line);min-width:0}fieldset label+label{margin-top:.6rem}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.95rem}th,td{text-align:left;padding:.7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{background:var(--paper)}caption{text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.5rem}.table-scroll input{max-width:130px}.sr-only{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0)}#validation,#scenario-errors{color:#9b2c13}button{font:inherit;cursor:pointer} .prose details{margin-bottom:1rem}.prose details p{margin-top:.7rem}
 @media(max-width:800px){.calc-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.results{position:static}.scenario-inputs{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:460px){.inputs{grid-template-columns:1fr}dl{font-size:.92rem;gap:.6rem}.advanced{padding:.9rem}.calc-area .actions{gap:.6rem}.calc-area button{width:100%}}
 @media print{.site-header,.site-footer,.consent-banner,.breadcrumbs,.actions{display:none!important}.calc-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.inputs{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.section{padding:1rem 0}.page-head{padding:1rem 0}h1{font-size:2rem}.advanced{break-inside:avoid}.wrap{width:100%}}
</style>
